#: src/maintainers/labels.md
msgid "Explicit maintainer or governance hold on a PR. Use it with `status:blocked` when a PR is held by an external dependency, policy decision, or prerequisite that GitHub's native review and check state does not enforce, especially when the PR otherwise appears mergeable. When applying it, leave a PR comment that names the blocker, the condition for removing `do-not-merge` and any companion blocked label, and the checks required before merge; reviews and linked issues may support that record but do not replace it. Pair it with `needs-maintainer-review` when a high-risk PR is explicitly routed for another independent Core Team approval. Use it for future-line work that must not land on the active release line. Do not apply it merely for pending CI, draft state, a behind branch, ordinary review, or active `CHANGES_REQUESTED`. Remove it only after the recorded condition clears and a maintainer rechecks the current native review state, required checks, mergeability, [Definition of Done](./pr-workflow.md#definition-of-done-dod), and [merge checklist](./pr-workflow.md#maintainer-merge-checklist)."
msgstr "对 PR 施加明确的维护者或治理阻塞。当 PR 因外部依赖、政策决策或 GitHub 原生评审和检查状态无法强制执行的先决条件而被暂缓时，请将其与 `status:blocked` 一起使用，尤其是在该 PR 看起来本来可以合并的情况下。应用此标签时，请留下 PR 评论，写明阻塞因素、移除 `do-not-merge` 及任何配套阻塞标签的条件，以及合并前所需的检查；评审和关联 issue 可以作为该记录的佐证，但不能替代它。对于明确转交给另一位独立 Core Team 成员审批的高风险 PR，请将其与 `needs-maintainer-review` 配合使用。对于必须不能进入当前活动发布线的未来版本线工作，请使用它。不要仅因 CI 待处理、草稿状态、分支落后、常规评审或当前处于 `CHANGES_REQUESTED` 而应用它。仅当记录的条件已满足，并且维护者重新检查当前原生评审状态、必需检查、可合并性、[Definition of Done](./pr-workflow.md#definition-of-done-dod) 和 [merge checklist](./pr-workflow.md#maintainer-merge-checklist) 后，才将其移除。"

