#: src/foundations/fnd-006-zero-compromise-in-practice.md
msgid "Structured logging and meaningful span design are not style preferences. They are what make the observability infrastructure you have actually useful, not just during development, but in the hands of users running ZeroClaw on hardware you will never see, in configurations you did not anticipate, encountering errors you did not plan for. The infrastructure creates the capability. The discipline in how contributors use it determines whether that capability translates into diagnosable systems."
msgstr "结构化日志记录和有意义的 span 设计并非风格偏好。它们是让你现有的可观测性基础设施真正发挥作用的关键，不仅在开发期间如此，在用户手中同样如此——这些用户在你永远无法看到的硬件上、在你未曾预料的配置中运行 ZeroClaw，并遭遇你未曾计划应对的错误。基础设施提供了能力，而贡献者使用它的规范程度决定了这种能力能否转化为可诊断的系统。"

