msgid "The trait definitions are the source of truth for exact methods, defaults, and types. The generated rustdoc is the navigable reference built from them. Use [Architecture → Overview](./architecture/overview.md#core-traits) for the curated extension families and [ADR-002](./architecture/decisions/ADR-002-trait-driven-extensibility.md) for the accepted trait-driven boundary decision."
msgstr "trait 定义是方法、默认值和类型的权威来源。生成的 rustdoc 是基于这些定义构建的可导航参考。请使用 [架构 → 概览](./architecture/overview.md#core-traits) 查看经过整理的扩展系列，并使用 [ADR-002](./architecture/decisions/ADR-002-trait-driven-extensibility.md) 了解已采纳的 trait 驱动边界决策。"

#: src/foundations/fnd-006-zero-compromise-in-practice.md
msgid "The trait layer in `zeroclaw-api` is the right architecture. `Provider`, `Channel`, `Tool`, `Memory`, `Observer`, `RuntimeAdapter`, and `Peripheral` are clean, well-reasoned abstractions. They are the right seams. The problem is not the design. It is that the design is not yet fully expressed in documentation, test coverage, and error handling discipline. This RFC is about closing that gap."
msgstr "`zeroclaw-api` 中的 trait 层架构设计是正确的。`Provider`、`Channel`、`Tool`、`Memory`、`Observer`、`RuntimeAdapter` 和 `Peripheral` 都是清晰、合理的抽象。它们是恰当的接缝。问题不在于设计本身，而在于该设计尚未在文档、测试覆盖率和错误处理规范中得到充分体现。本 RFC 旨在弥合这一差距。"

