#: src/contributing/communication.md
msgid "Use a GitHub handoff when Discord produces something the project must remember. Create or update an issue, discussion, PR comment, or maintainer doc when the thread produces a reproducible bug, concrete feature scope, architecture or governance decision, maintainer commitment, owner assignment, milestone decision, blocker, workaround, validation evidence, release-impact note, or stale-exemption reason. The handoff only needs the decision, evidence, owner when one exists, and enough context for another maintainer to continue without rereading chat."
msgstr "当 Discord 产生项目必须记录的内容时，使用 GitHub 进行交接。当讨论串产生可复现的 bug、具体的功能范围、架构或治理决策、维护者承诺、负责人分配、里程碑决策、阻塞项、临时解决方案、验证证据、发布影响说明或过期豁免原因时，创建或更新 issue、discussion、PR 评论或维护者文档。交接内容只需包含决策、证据、负责人（如有），以及足够的上下文，使另一位维护者无需重读聊天记录即可继续工作。"

#: src/tools/python-skills.md
msgid "Use a custom Docker runtime image when you need repeatable dependencies, production packaging, or an explicit container boundary for built-in shell calls."
msgstr "当你需要可复现的依赖项、生产环境打包，或为内置 shell 调用设置明确的容器边界时，请使用自定义 Docker 运行时镜像。"

#: src/sop/fan-in/overview.md
msgid "Use a live source ([MQTT](./mqtt.md), [Filesystem](./filesystem.md), [AMQP](./amqp.md)) or start the run with [`sop_execute`](./manual.md)"
msgstr "使用实时源（[MQTT](./mqtt.md)、[Filesystem](./filesystem.md)、[AMQP](./amqp.md)）或使用 [`sop_execute`](./manual.md) 启动运行"

#: src/sop/fan-in/manual.md
msgid "Use a manual trigger when the decision to run belongs to the agent's reasoning rather than to an external signal. This is the path the [worked example](../example.md) uses: a release arrives over a channel, the agent reasons about it, and then fires the SOP itself."
msgstr "当执行与否的决定属于代理的推理而不是外部信号时，请使用手动触发器。这是 [worked example](../example.md) 所采用的路径：一个发布通过某个渠道到达，代理对其进行推理，然后自行触发 SOP。"

#: src/channels/telegram.md
msgid "Use a type-wide `channel = \"telegram\"` only when the same identities should be accepted by every configured Telegram alias. For the complete schema and resolution rules, see [Peer Groups](./peer-groups.md)."
msgstr "仅当相同的身份应被每个已配置的 Telegram 别名接受时，才在类型范围内使用 `channel = \"telegram\"`。有关完整的架构和解析规则，请参阅 [Peer Groups](./peer-groups.md)。"

#: src/setup/service.md
msgid "Use a user-service override when the daemon needs environment variables that are not present in your interactive shell:"
msgstr "当守护进程需要交互式 shell 中不存在的环境变量时，请使用用户服务覆盖："

#: src/maintainers/labels.md
msgid "Use assignees for active work. Use issue comments, issue body sections, public fields, or linked trackers for routing evidence when a special stale, tracker, or deferred-decision state needs explanation. `status:blocked` uses the recorded-blocker rule. The [Project board contract](./pr-workflow.md#issue-routing-evidence) defines the accepted evidence sources and routing outcomes."
msgstr "为正在进行的工作使用 assignees。当需要解释特殊的搁置、跟踪器或延期决策状态时，使用 issue 评论、issue 正文部分、公共字段或关联的跟踪器作为路由依据。`status:blocked` 采用已记录的阻塞项规则。[项目看板约定](./pr-workflow.md#issue-routing-evidence)定义了可接受的依据来源和路由结果。"

#: src/tools/skills.md
msgid "Use bundles for skills an agent should load during runtime. A bundle is configured under `[skill_bundles.<alias>]`; when its `directory` is omitted, ZeroClaw resolves it to `<install>/shared/skills/<alias>/`."
msgstr "在运行时，智能体应加载的技能请使用 bundles。bundle 在 `[skill_bundles.<alias>]` 下进行配置；当省略其 `directory` 时，ZeroClaw 会将其解析为 `<install>/shared/skills/<alias>/`。"

#: src/hardware/hardware-peripherals-design.md src/contributing/privacy.md
